Subject: Guard bool/true/false/nullptr macros against C23

C23 promotes `bool`, `true`, `false` and `nullptr` from library macros to
keywords. libmdbx still defines all four for the C build, guarded only by
`#ifndef bool` / `!defined(nullptr)` -- which stay true in C23, because a
keyword is not a macro. clang then reports

    mdbx.h:417:9: warning: keyword is hidden by macro definition [-Wkeyword-macro]
    mdbx.h:420:9: ...
    mdbx.h:423:9: ...
    mdbx-internals.h:361:9: ...

which `R CMD check` classifies as significant warnings. CRAN's Debian clang
leg compiles as C23 (clang defaults to gnu23 from clang 23), so this is a
WARNING on an incoming submission; it does not fire under gcc, which has no
such diagnostic, nor in C17 mode.

Add the missing standard-version clause to each guard, so the macros are
defined exactly where they are still needed and omitted where the compiler
already supplies the keyword. Every definition matched the C23 semantics it
now defers to (`_Bool`, 1, 0, a null pointer constant), so no generated code
changes. Verified: `clang -S -O2` of mdbx.c against the patched and unpatched
headers is byte-identical under both -std=gnu17 (where the macros survive) and
-std=gnu23 (where they are now dropped in favour of the keywords), modulo the
`__TIME__` stamp libmdbx embeds in its build string.

Rejected alternative: `-Wno-keyword-macro` in PKG_CFLAGS. Writing R Extensions
treats -Wno-* as non-portable, and it would trade this WARNING for a "checking
compilation flags used" one -- the same trade rejected in patch 4.

Rejected alternative: `SystemRequirements: C17`, which pins the whole package
back to a standard CRAN is actively moving off, to avoid a diagnostic about
four lines.

Not yet upstream: libmdbx master carries the same code at the same lines as of
v0.14.3. Worth sending, and worth re-checking on the next version bump.

--- a/src/vendor/libmdbx/mdbx.h
+++ b/src/vendor/libmdbx/mdbx.h
@@ -412,7 +412,8 @@
 
 /*----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
 
-#ifndef __cplusplus
+/* R package patch: C23 makes bool/true/false keywords. See tools/patches. */
+#if !defined(__cplusplus) && (!defined(__STDC_VERSION__) || __STDC_VERSION__ < 202311L)
 #ifndef bool
 #define bool _Bool
 #endif
@@ -422,7 +423,7 @@
 #ifndef false
 #define false (0)
 #endif
-#endif /* bool without __cplusplus */
+#endif /* bool without __cplusplus, before C23 */
 
 /** Workaround for old compilers without support for C++17 `noexcept`. */
 #if defined(DOXYGEN)
--- a/src/vendor/libmdbx/mdbx-internals.h
+++ b/src/vendor/libmdbx/mdbx-internals.h
@@ -357,7 +357,9 @@
 #endif
 #endif /* __extern_C */
 
-#if !defined(nullptr) && (!defined(__cplusplus) || (__cplusplus < 201103L && !defined(_MSC_VER)))
+/* R package patch: C23 makes nullptr a keyword. See tools/patches. */
+#if !defined(nullptr) && (!defined(__cplusplus) || (__cplusplus < 201103L && !defined(_MSC_VER))) &&                    \
+    (defined(__cplusplus) || !defined(__STDC_VERSION__) || __STDC_VERSION__ < 202311L)
 #define nullptr NULL
 #endif
 
